{
  "$comment": "How a mount table is resolved from a committed declaration and the .mounts.json hierarchy. The engine (SourceMounts_test.cpp) and the editor (MountTableCasesTests) both run every case, so the two readers cannot drift. Paths are relative to a case folder whose own .mounts.json has \"root\": true; ${temp} in a path is that folder. A cooked source (cooked_sources) is built from its recipe by each harness's own fixture writer: path, kind (loose or pak), roots (the mounts its virtual paths start with; a pak names exactly one, its mount), assets (each a virtual path and an asset type it provides, keyed from the path), requirements (a pak's: each a mount, and the virtual path and type of the asset it requires of it), external_script (a script with an external source under its first root; a loose root only) and format (current, or unsupported: a version this build cannot read). Mounts compare by name; codes compare as sets.",
  "schema_version": 2,
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "committed relative path",
      "folders": ["ws/proj/Content"],
      "declarations": [
        { "name": "Content", "kind": "Source", "path": "Content" }
      ],
      "mounts": [
        {
          "name": "Content",
          "kind": "Source",
          "scope": "declared",
          "state": "Bound",
          "origin": "committed",
          "folder": "ws/proj/Content",
          "role": "Own"
        }
      ],
      "codes": []
    },
    {
